        "Najash (fake bidding to inflate a price without intent to buy, manipulating other buyers) is explicitly prohibited and its practitioner cursed as 'a cursed taker of Riba'.",
        "Khalabah (misleading marketing — overprojecting a commodity's quality) is prohibited as deception; excessive oath-swearing while selling is discouraged for the same reason.",
        "Deceiving a Mustarsal (an unknowing/naive market entrant) is described as being equivalent in severity to Riba — an unusually strong equation used to stress the gravity of exploiting an information-disadvantaged buyer.",
        "Banks (managing public funds as a trust) may impose penalty fines on wilful defaulters as a deterrent, with proceeds directed to charity, not the bank's own profit — distinct from the individual-level virtue of waiving a genuinely destitute debtor's obligation."
